From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Weber <doweb85@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:51:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/27] byteplan: full threadgroups for small Metal ops,
 delta-net state read in place

Decode and draft checks ran several Metal kernels with one thread per threadgroup:
ssm_conv (one threadgroup per channel), unary ops below 32k elements and binary
row-broadcast ops below 64k elements (one threadgroup per element). They now run
256 threads per threadgroup with the same per-element arithmetic, so the results
stay bit-identical (ssm_conv in a verify step: 52 -> 6 us).

ggml_gated_delta_net_ids reads each sequence's initial state from its row of the
whole state cache (ids from build_rs), like ggml_ssm_scan does for Mamba, so
qwen4exp no longer gathers a 3 MB state copy per delta-net layer in every graph.
CPU and Metal implement the ids; without ids nothing changes.

Measured on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next with MTP + n-gram drafts (ABBA, same answers):
agent work, new code and prose +6 to +7 %, code edits +4 %.
